 "slice_mm_basis": "the source gives slices of 1.0 mm at a collimation of 0.75 mm overlapping by 0.25 mm, and numbers them 58 to 285 from the proximal end; 0.5 mm a slice makes that 113.5 mm against a bone of 113.6 mm, and puts the two complete holes 34 mm apart against the 35 mm measured with calipers",
 "orientation": "posterior (the side with holes 1 to 3) is up in the figures, so LM is across and AP is up and down",
 "edges": "the silhouettes are wider than the bone: at its narrowest the shaft measures 24.5 by 18.1 mm here against 23.5 by 17.0 mm with calipers (turk1997), which is 0.5 mm on each surface; the walls and the holes' widths against the source's own CT values give 0.4 to 1.0 mm. bonepipe.geometry takes this as the parameter edge_mm",
